    {
      "Seq": 17,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 5,
      "Place": "Plain",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 1824,
      "Actor": "Nyccolhoth Lhavyniwyn",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I find myself at noon in the village square, where my days spent at the stable now echo the foot-traffic crossing every direction. The well, the ways, the peat cut, and the mounting block still stand, their presence a silent reminder of lessons learned. I watch a well, a central stone-rimmed well at the square's heart, a wooden bucket on its rope. Childhood memories of saving coins and dreams of fortune echo here, as I once pushed through a storm with worn legs.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 4,
      "Block": 0,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 18,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 5,
      "Place": "Plain",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 1824,
      "Actor": "Nyccolhoth Lhavyniwyn",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I spy a green edge, waterside, and threshing floor. To the orchard, I march, relying on sturdy arms and a hearty laugh to lighten the load.",
