    {
      "Seq": 26,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 5,
      "Place": "Plain",
      "Area": "Village Orchard",
      "LocationId": 1824,
      "Actor": "Nyccolhoth Lhavyniwyn",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I walk through the grass, the scent of the goat's breath heavy in my nose. My body tenses at the warning in its posture, a kinship to all creatures. The waterside whispers, the old man's hands warm and familiar, the forge's fire crackling, but my focus remains on the goat's flicked ear, a silent command. I catch the scent of ripe apples, the posture of an old tree wary, as branches hold heavy with fruit. It warns, a beast's kin, ready to move if danger nears.",
